```

**Problem**: When multiple concurrent requests hit a cache miss, each one calls fetchFn() before any sets the cache. With 100 concurrent requests on cold cache, all 100 fetch data.

#### 2. Missing Await on Async Function
**File**: src/services/cache.ts:7
**Impact**: Critical (caches Promise, not result)
**Pattern**: Async Bug

**Current Code**:
```typescript
const data = fetchFn();  // Returns Promise, not data!
cache.set(key, data);
```

**Problem**: fetchFn is async but not awaited. Caches the Promise instead of the resolved value.

**Recommended Fix**:
```typescript
const cache = new Map<string, any>();
const pending = new Map<string, Promise<any>>();

async function getCachedData<T>(
  key: string, 
  fetchFn: () => Promise<T>,
  ttlMs: number = 60000
): Promise<T> {
  // Check cache first
  const cached = cache.get(key);
  if (cached && cached.expiresAt > Date.now()) {
    return cached.data;
  }

  // Check if already fetching (prevent stampede)
  if (pending.has(key)) {
    return pending.get(key)!;
  }

  // Fetch and cache
  const promise = fetchFn().then(data => {
    cache.set(key, { data, expiresAt: Date.now() + ttlMs });
    pending.delete(key);
    return data;
  }).catch(err => {
    pending.delete(key);
    throw err;
  });

  pending.set(key, promise);
  return promise;
}
```

